From: Yaron Shahrabani <yarons@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] android: Mark the result metadata as complete whenever it is sent

A request with a failed buffer (for example a JPEG that could not be
encoded) was completed with result metadata but partial_result = 0. The
camera service refuses that ("Result is malformed ... partial_result 0 must
be 1 if partial result is not supported") and turns a recoverable buffer
error into ERROR_CAMERA_DEVICE, which closes the camera.
---
--- a/src/android/camera_device.cpp
+++ b/src/android/camera_device.cpp
@@ -1390,7 +1390,13 @@
 		captureResult.num_output_buffers = resultBuffers.size();
 		captureResult.output_buffers = resultBuffers.data();
 
-		if (descriptor->status_ == Camera3RequestDescriptor::Status::Success)
+		/*
+		 * The result metadata is complete whenever it is sent, also
+		 * for a request with a failed buffer. Leaving partial_result at
+		 * 0 then makes the camera service drop the result as malformed
+		 * and report a fatal device error.
+		 */
+		if (captureResult.result)
 			captureResult.partial_result = 1;
 
 		callbacks_->process_capture_result(callbacks_, &captureResult);
